<VI _name="Spike Input Injection.vi" description="Decisive spike for the RemoteVI input path (docs/protocol.md section 4): can a LabVIEW front panel be operated by POSTING Win32 window messages to its window\2C with no real mouse and the window possibly in the background? Starts Injection Fixture.vi (FP.Open with Activate as given\2C Run VI without waiting)\2C optionally covers it with the panel of Blocker Path so it is NOT the foreground window\2C then a) clicks Switch\2C b) drags Slide\2C c) types into Number\2C d) types into Text and clicks away\2C e) clicks the latched Stop and times how long until the VI is Idle. Uses the message recipes the spike established: drag moves and button-up carry SCREEN coordinates in lParam\2C and each WM_CHAR is wrapped in WM_KEYDOWN/UP of a key with no character (VK 0xE8) - each checked by reading the value back through VI Server. Reports pass/fail and the observed values per step\2C whether the fixture panel was frontmost\2C and the total time. Cleanup (abort if still running\2C close panel and reference) always runs.">
